{"title":"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Some_More_Calculation,_by_DARSHSHETTY4)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Some More Calculation, by DARSHSHETTY4)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Patio blocks that are hexagons <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> unit on a side are used to outline a garden by placing the blocks edge to edge with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> on each side. The diagram indicates the path of blocks around the garden when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/e/84e75ddd39b9408f4d8e7fa62d2f6cdca00232de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AIME_2002_II_Problem_4.gif\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/1/12/AIME_2002_II_Problem_4.gif\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"375\" height=\"418\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/5/185d026ddfd892ea36f6c34aba6db94844ac445c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=202$\" width=\"61\" height=\"12\" />, then the area of the garden enclosed by the path, not including the path itself, is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/a/86a04561712e75595b34f72025894c34a19b9be2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\left(\\sqrt3/2\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"79\" height=\"32\" /> square units, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is a positive integer. Find the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/2/65262bf247c4a3c6114a8223d249dc9702619d3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" />, the path of blocks has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/e/49e81ca21bb6fc7fea56c4f60f7cf68c5046caac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6(n-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" /> blocks total in it. When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/9/1d96ecc15129c5631ba4a2c6578e91e3d13e3baf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, there is just one lonely block. Thus, the area of the garden enclosed by the path when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/5/185d026ddfd892ea36f6c34aba6db94844ac445c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=202$\" width=\"61\" height=\"12\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/a/ecad98b857944eb31fe872e4829687a8ce265342.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(1+6+12+18+\\cdots +1200)A=(1+6(1+2+3...+200))A\\]\" width=\"478\" height=\"18\" />,\n</p><p>where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is the area of one block. Then, because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/4/3c4dc0cb9604dc0b2e470d33b0e484c3c0643941.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n(n+1)/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" /> is equal to the sum of the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> integers:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/1/2319ef0a32ca4887a6f58234c250d5689530db33.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(1+6(1+2+3...+200))=(1+6((200)(201)/2))A=120601A\\]\" width=\"478\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/4/99459dcd6a3acf0ad5c29cec78b4168d781ef5f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=\\dfrac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"73\" height=\"41\" />, the area of the garden is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/8/1283821e2343826447216d84e3c55534912c388c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[120601\\cdot \\dfrac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2}=\\dfrac{361803\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\]\" width=\"209\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/e/6fe367c142f6d10f7538b9fbe3853d6d52a437bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=361803$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"93\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/1/1f17224101139acf19ef3868758f96796bc1f902.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{m}{1000}=361$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"90\" height=\"33\" /> Remainder <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/4/9b4326afa39068f7944b34cb3bd8da58e4ad9402.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{803}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that this is just the definition for a centered hexagonal number, and  the formula for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/1/5f1ff42ff9de1c2c24f161f5bf4dc46a0e9b9950.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n-1)^{th}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"20\" /> term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/f/73f5a51e8cd2ef8679586a637d1838e8f8d5f59e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3n(n+1)+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"106\" height=\"18\" />. Applying this for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/3/8f37626d49b4082c9102bf930bca51277ff2eb43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> as we want the inner area gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/a/6ea5cb8fae504bba05c87602453eeac616e8f549.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$120601$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"53\" height=\"13\" />. Then continue as above.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Some_More_Calculation.2C_by_DARSHSHETTY4.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Some_More_Calculation,_by_DARSHSHETTY4)\">Solution 3 (Some More Calculation, by DARSHSHETTY4)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Some More Calculation, by DARSHSHETTY4)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>You can also find the area of the inside of the garden by constructing a larger hexagon using segments connected to the centers of each of the \"vertex\" mini-hexagons. \n</p><p>So, the side length of the larger constructed hexagon is (202-2) * √3 + √3/2 + √3/2 or 201 * √3. \n</p><p>So, the area of the larger constructed hexagon is (201*√3)^2 * 3 * √3/2. \n</p><p>Now, we need to find the area of the smaller hexagons that are between the garden boundary and the constructed hexagon boundary. \nThe area of the side length's hexagons per side length are 202-2 * 3√3 / 2 / 2, or 200 * 3/2 * √3/2, and extrapolating it to the whole hexagon, it is 6 * 200 * 3/2 * √3/2. \n</p><p>Now, we need to account for the areas of the vertex hexagons. The segments create 90 degree angles on 2 sides of the hexagon, creating 2 30 60 90 right triangles (leg 1/2, √3/2 and 1 equilateral triangle (side length 1). \n</p><p><br />\nSo, the sum of the vertex hexagon areas are 6 * ((1^2 * √3/4) +√3/8 + √3/8). Hence, having the 2nd and 3rd expressions subtracted from the first, we get 361803 * √3/2, so the remainder is 803.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II\" title=\"2002 AIME II\">2002 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2002 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2002\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2002 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017195658\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.037 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.058 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 212/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1806/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 128/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4617/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.548      1 -total\n 57.68%    7.238      1 Template:AIME_box\n 39.83%    4.998      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:3125:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017195658 and revision id 282806. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}